IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), PART III.1, Division 3 Entitlement, second half: regs 76.19, 76.2 and
-- 76.21 (how weeks of provincial benefits count against the maximum weeks, and how weeks are shared by two persons caring
-- for the same child under different regimes). Layer 1 (the law, objectively), piece er4. Unofficial plain-text rendering;
-- nothing here is "verified against the official text". No section GIVEN: every rule has its own GIVEN.
--
-- THE RELATIONS. The weeks of provincial benefits a claimant has been paid count as weeks under the Act (76.19(1)), so they
-- use up the maximum weeks of s 12 of the Act (out of range: Act s 12, piece ei1; the maxima are inputs). Weeks paid
-- at an accelerated rate are converted to the weeks they represent (76.19(2), (3)). Where two persons caring for the
-- same child live in different provinces, one claiming under s 23 of the Act (the "claimant") and the other provincial
-- benefits (the "provincial applicant"), the claimant's weeks are halved unless they agree otherwise (76.21).
-- Weeks are NUMBERs of weeks. The three figures of the Act that the formulas read (the 35 and 61 of s 12(3)(b), the 40
-- of s 12(4)(b)(i)) are inputs, never written in a rule.

§ `Regulation 76.19 -- payment of benefits`

§§ `Regulation 76.19(1) -- provincial weeks count as weeks under the Act`

-- src:1247 | 76.19 (1) Subject to subsection (2), the provincial benefits paid to a claimant in respect of a week in a benefit period are considered to be benefits paid in respect of a week under the Act if the claimant would have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits under the Act, and any week in respect of which the claimant receives provincial benefits counts as a week for the purpose of calculating
-- src:1248 | (a) the overall maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period under paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act taken together; and
-- src:1249 | (b) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid under subsection 12(4) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.19(1) (src:1247-1249)
GIVEN `the claimant would have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.19(1) the provincial benefits paid for the week are considered to be benefits paid in respect of a week under the Act` IF
    `the claimant would have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits under the Act`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.19(1)(a) (src:1247-1248)
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.19(1)(a) the weeks counted toward the overall maximum number of weeks under paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act taken together` MEANS
    `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` PLUS `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act`

-- The weeks left within a maximum (out of range: Act s 12, piece ei1): the maximum less the weeks counted. The text does
-- not say what happens when more weeks have been counted than the maximum allows: NOTHING.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.19(1)(a) (src:1247-1248)
GIVEN `the overall maximum number of weeks under paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act taken together` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.19(1)(a) the weeks left within the overall maximum` MEANS
    IF `reg 76.19(1)(a) the weeks counted toward the overall maximum number of weeks under paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act taken together` `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act`
           AT MOST `the overall maximum number of weeks under paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act taken together`
    THEN JUST (`the overall maximum number of weeks under paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act taken together`
                   MINUS `reg 76.19(1)(a) the weeks counted toward the overall maximum number of weeks under paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act taken together` `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act`)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.19(1)(b) (src:1247, 1249)
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.19(1)(b) the weeks counted toward the maximum number of weeks under subsection 12(4) of the Act` MEANS
    `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` PLUS `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.19(1)(b) (src:1247, 1249)
GIVEN `the maximum number of weeks under subsection 12(4) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.19(1)(b) the weeks left within the maximum under subsection 12(4)` MEANS
    IF `reg 76.19(1)(b) the weeks counted toward the maximum number of weeks under subsection 12(4) of the Act` `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act`
           AT MOST `the maximum number of weeks under subsection 12(4) of the Act`
    THEN JUST (`the maximum number of weeks under subsection 12(4) of the Act`
                   MINUS `reg 76.19(1)(b) the weeks counted toward the maximum number of weeks under subsection 12(4) of the Act` `the weeks of benefits paid under the Act` `the weeks of provincial benefits that count as weeks under the Act`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 76.19(1.1) -- the benefit period`

-- A benefit period established under a provincial law is deemed to be a benefit period under the Act; it is deemed to
-- have begun the same week "if the claimant would have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits under the Act
-- in respect of the same period" (the condition qualifies the second limb only, fork F21).
-- src:1250 | (1.1) A benefit period is deemed to be established when a benefit period was established under a provincial law, and it is deemed to have begun the same week as the period established under the provincial law if the claimant would have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits under the Act in respect of the same period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.19(1.1) (src:1250)
GIVEN `a benefit period was established under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.19(1.1) a benefit period is deemed to be established` IF
    `a benefit period was established under a provincial law`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.19(1.1) (src:1250)
GIVEN `a benefit period was established under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first week of the period established under the provincial law` IS A DATE
      `the claimant would have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits under the Act in respect of the same period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 76.19(1.1) the week in which the benefit period is deemed to have begun` MEANS
    IF     `a benefit period was established under a provincial law`
       AND `the claimant would have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits under the Act in respect of the same period`
    THEN JUST `the first week of the period established under the provincial law`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulations 76.19(2) and (3) -- benefits paid at an accelerated rate`

-- Weeks paid times (the maximum weeks at the non-accelerated rate divided by the maximum weeks at the accelerated rate).
-- A maximum at the accelerated rate that is not above zero gives no ratio: NOTHING.
-- src:1251 | (2) Where a provincial plan provides for the optional payment of provincial benefits at an accelerated rate, such that the maximum amount of a particular type of provincial benefit payable under the plan may be paid to the claimant over fewer weeks, and the claimant is paid those benefits at the accelerated rate, the number of weeks of benefits that those weeks of provincial benefits represent under the Act shall be determined by multiplying the number of weeks of the particular type of provincial benefits paid to the claimant by the result obtained by dividing the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the nonaccelerated rate by the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the accelerated rate.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.19(2) (src:1251)
GIVEN `the weeks of the particular type of provincial benefits paid to the claimant` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the non-accelerated rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the accelerated rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.19(2) the number of weeks of benefits that the weeks of provincial benefits represent under the Act, before rounding` MEANS
    IF `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the accelerated rate` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the weeks of the particular type of provincial benefits paid to the claimant`
                   TIMES (`the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the non-accelerated rate` DIVIDED BY `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the accelerated rate`))

-- src:1252 | (3) If the determination of the number of weeks under subsection (2) results in a number that contains a fraction of a week, the number shall be rounded to the nearest multiple of one week or, if the amount is equidistant from two multiples of one week, to the higher multiple.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.19(3) (src:1252)
GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.19(3) the number of weeks rounded to the nearest multiple of one week, the higher multiple when equidistant` MEANS
    FLOOR (weeks PLUS 0.5)

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.19(2) (src:1251)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.19(3) (src:1252)
GIVEN `the claimant is paid the provincial benefits at the accelerated rate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weeks of the particular type of provincial benefits paid to the claimant` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the non-accelerated rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the accelerated rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.19(2) and (3) the weeks of provincial benefits as weeks under the Act` MEANS
    IF `the claimant is paid the provincial benefits at the accelerated rate`
    THEN CONSIDER `reg 76.19(2) the number of weeks of benefits that the weeks of provincial benefits represent under the Act, before rounding`
                      `the weeks of the particular type of provincial benefits paid to the claimant`
                      `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the non-accelerated rate`
                      `the maximum number of such weeks of benefits payable at the accelerated rate`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST represented THEN JUST (`reg 76.19(3) the number of weeks rounded to the nearest multiple of one week, the higher multiple when equidistant` represented)
    ELSE JUST `the weeks of the particular type of provincial benefits paid to the claimant`

§ `Regulation 76.2 -- weeks of provincial benefits beyond the maximum under the Act`

-- If the Act's maximum for the reason (12(3)(a) or (b), 12(4)(a) or (b)) is less than the weeks the province pays, "the excess number
-- of weeks for which provincial benefits may be paid" are not taken into account; the weeks paid that are taken into account
-- are therefore at most the Act's maximum.
-- src:1253 | 76.2 If the maximum number of weeks referred to in paragraph 12(3)(a) or (b) or (4)(a) or (b) of the Act is less than the maximum number of weeks for which the corresponding types of benefits may be paid under a provincial plan, the excess number of weeks for which provincial benefits may be paid shall not be taken into account for the purpose of determining the maximum number of weeks referred to in that paragraph.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.2 (src:1253)
GIVEN `the maximum number of weeks under the Act for the reason` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of weeks for which the corresponding types of provincial benefits may be paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of provincial benefits paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.2 the weeks of provincial benefits that are taken into account in determining the maximum number of weeks` MEANS
    IF `the maximum number of weeks under the Act for the reason` LESS THAN `the maximum number of weeks for which the corresponding types of provincial benefits may be paid`
    THEN min `the weeks of provincial benefits paid` (`the maximum number of weeks for which the corresponding types of provincial benefits may be paid` MINUS excess)
    ELSE `the weeks of provincial benefits paid`
    WHERE
        excess MEANS `the maximum number of weeks for which the corresponding types of provincial benefits may be paid` MINUS `the maximum number of weeks under the Act for the reason`

§ `Regulation 76.21 -- persons making claims under different regimes`

§§ `Regulation 76.21(1) -- when the sharing applies`

-- src:1256 | 76.21 (1) Subsection (2) applies in respect of two persons who are caring for the same child or children and who do not reside in the same province at the time the first one of them makes an application under section 22 or 23 of the Act or an application for provincial benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.21(1) (src:1256)
GIVEN `two persons are caring for the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they do not reside in the same province at the time the first one of them makes an application under section 22 or 23 of the Act or an application for provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.21(1) subsection (2) applies in respect of the two persons` IF
        `two persons are caring for the same child or children`
    AND `they do not reside in the same province at the time the first one of them makes an application under section 22 or 23 of the Act or an application for provincial benefits`

§§ `Regulation 76.21(2) -- the claimant's share of the weeks`

-- Unless the two persons have agreed on the number of weeks each will apply for, or a court has ordered how to share
-- them: then the number is theirs (or the court's), and the subsection gives none: NOTHING. Otherwise an even number of
-- weeks is halved; an odd number gives the claimant one week plus half the rest if the claimant applied first, and half
-- the rest (the number less one week) if the provincial applicant applied first.
-- src:1257 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), where one of the two persons referred to in subsection (1) has applied for and is entitled to receive benefits under section 23 of the Act (referred to in this section as “the claimant”) and the other person has applied for and is entitled to receive provincial benefits (referred to in this section as “the provincial applicant”), unless they have entered into an agreement as to the number of weeks of such benefits they will each respectively apply for or there is a court order respecting the sharing of those weeks of benefits,
-- src:1258 | (a) if the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant would otherwise be entitled to receive under section 23 of the Act is an even number, the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant is half that number; and
-- src:1259 | (b) if that number is an odd number,
-- src:1260 | (i) where the claimant made the earlier application, one week of those benefits plus half of the remaining weeks of benefits is payable to the claimant, and
-- src:1261 | (ii) where the provincial applicant made the earlier application, half the number of weeks of benefits remaining, after deducting one week, are payable to the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.21(2) (src:1257-1261)
GIVEN `the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant would otherwise be entitled to receive under section 23 of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `who made the earlier application` IS A `er4 Who made the earlier application`
      `the two persons have entered into an agreement as to the number of weeks they will each apply for, or there is a court order respecting the sharing of those weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.21(2) the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant, subject to subsection (3)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the two persons have entered into an agreement as to the number of weeks they will each apply for, or there is a court order respecting the sharing of those weeks`
             THEN NOTHING
           IF `the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant would otherwise be entitled to receive under section 23 of the Act` MODULO 2 EQUALS 0
             THEN JUST (`the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant would otherwise be entitled to receive under section 23 of the Act` DIVIDED BY 2)
           IF `who made the earlier application` EQUALS `er4 the person claiming benefits under the Act made the earlier application`
             THEN JUST (1 PLUS ((`the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant would otherwise be entitled to receive under section 23 of the Act` MINUS 1) DIVIDED BY 2))
           OTHERWISE JUST ((`the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant would otherwise be entitled to receive under section 23 of the Act` MINUS 1) DIVIDED BY 2)

§§ `Regulation 76.21(3) -- the most weeks that may be paid to the claimant`

-- A, B, C and D are the formula's own letters. A is the maximum weeks of s 12(4)(b)(i) when the weeks are divided (40 in
-- the Act); B is the weeks of provincial benefits paid to the provincial applicant, converted by reg 76.19(2) and (3)
-- where they were paid at an accelerated rate; C is the 61 weeks of s 12(3)(b)(ii) and D the 35 weeks of s 12(3)(b)(i).
-- All are inputs (out of range: Act s 12, piece ei1).
-- src:1262 | (3) The maximum number of weeks of benefits that may be paid to the claimant under section 23 of the Act shall not be greater than
-- src:1263 | (a) in the case of a claimant who has, under subsection 23(1.1) of the Act, elected to receive benefits for the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) of the Act, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(4)(b)(i) of the Act when the weeks of benefits are divided, less the number of weeks of provincial benefits that are paid to the provincial applicant, taking into account any weeks of provincial benefits that are paid at the accelerated rate referred to in subsection 76.19(2), if applicable; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.21(3)(a) (src:1262-1263)
GIVEN `A, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(4)(b)(i) of the Act when the weeks of benefits are divided` IS A NUMBER
      `B, the number of weeks of provincial benefits that are paid to the provincial applicant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.21(3)(a) the most weeks payable to a claimant who elected the 35-week maximum` MEANS
    `A, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(4)(b)(i) of the Act when the weeks of benefits are divided`
        MINUS `B, the number of weeks of provincial benefits that are paid to the provincial applicant`

-- Rounded down to the nearest whole number. A D that is not above zero gives no result: NOTHING.
-- src:1264 | (b) in the case of a claimant who has, under subsection 23(1.1) of the Act, elected to receive benefits for the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii) of the Act, the number of weeks, rounded down to the nearest whole number, determined by the following formula:
-- src:1265 | (A – B) × C/D
-- src:1266 | where:
-- src:1267 | A is the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(4)(b)(i) of the Act when the weeks of benefits are divided;
-- src:1268 | B is the number of weeks of provincial benefits that are paid to the provincial applicant, taking into account any weeks of provincial benefits that are paid at the accelerated rate referred to in subsection 76.19(2), if applicable;
-- src:1269 | C is the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii) of the Act; and
-- src:1270 | D is the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.21(3)(b) (src:1264-1270)
GIVEN `A, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(4)(b)(i) of the Act when the weeks of benefits are divided` IS A NUMBER
      `B, the number of weeks of provincial benefits that are paid to the provincial applicant` IS A NUMBER
      `C, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `D, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.21(3)(b) the most weeks payable to a claimant who elected the 61-week maximum` MEANS
    IF `D, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) of the Act` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (FLOOR (((`A, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(4)(b)(i) of the Act when the weeks of benefits are divided`
                         MINUS `B, the number of weeks of provincial benefits that are paid to the provincial applicant`)
                        TIMES `C, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii) of the Act`)
                       DIVIDED BY `D, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) of the Act`))

-- (3) by the claimant's election under subsection 23(1.1) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.21(3) (src:1262-1270)
GIVEN election IS A `Election of maximum weeks`
      `A, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(4)(b)(i) of the Act when the weeks of benefits are divided` IS A NUMBER
      `B, the number of weeks of provincial benefits that are paid to the provincial applicant` IS A NUMBER
      `C, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `D, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.21(3) the most weeks that may be paid to the claimant` MEANS
    CONSIDER election
    WHEN `the 35-week maximum` THEN
        JUST (`reg 76.21(3)(a) the most weeks payable to a claimant who elected the 35-week maximum`
                  `A, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(4)(b)(i) of the Act when the weeks of benefits are divided`
                  `B, the number of weeks of provincial benefits that are paid to the provincial applicant`)
    WHEN `the 61-week maximum` THEN
        `reg 76.21(3)(b) the most weeks payable to a claimant who elected the 61-week maximum`
            `A, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(4)(b)(i) of the Act when the weeks of benefits are divided`
            `B, the number of weeks of provincial benefits that are paid to the provincial applicant`
            `C, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii) of the Act`
            `D, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) of the Act`

§§ `Regulation 76.21(4) -- the maximum is the one elected`

-- (4) fixes the maximum for the claimant as the 35 or the 61 weeks of s 12(3)(b)(i) or (ii) according to the election; read with
-- (3) as a ceiling on the claimant's weeks (fork F20).
-- src:1271 | (4) The maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to a claimant under subsection (3) is the maximum number of weeks established under subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) or (ii) of the Act, in accordance with the election made under subsection 23(1.1) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.21(4) (src:1271)
GIVEN election IS A `Election of maximum weeks`
      `the maximum number of weeks established under subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of weeks established under subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.21(4) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to the claimant in accordance with the election` MEANS
    CONSIDER election
    WHEN `the 35-week maximum` THEN `the maximum number of weeks established under subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) of the Act`
    WHEN `the 61-week maximum` THEN `the maximum number of weeks established under subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii) of the Act`

§§ `Regulation 76.21 -- the weeks payable to the claimant`

-- The claimant's share under (2), kept within (3) and (4): the least of the three. Where the persons have agreed or a court
-- has ordered how to share, (2) gives no number and neither does this rule: NOTHING.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.21 (src:1256-1271)
GIVEN `the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant would otherwise be entitled to receive under section 23 of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `who made the earlier application` IS A `er4 Who made the earlier application`
      `the two persons have entered into an agreement as to the number of weeks they will each apply for, or there is a court order respecting the sharing of those weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
      election IS A `Election of maximum weeks`
      `A, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(4)(b)(i) of the Act when the weeks of benefits are divided` IS A NUMBER
      `B, the number of weeks of provincial benefits that are paid to the provincial applicant` IS A NUMBER
      `C, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `D, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 76.21 the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 76.21(2) the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant, subject to subsection (3)`
                 `the number of weeks of benefits that the claimant would otherwise be entitled to receive under section 23 of the Act`
                 `who made the earlier application`
                 `the two persons have entered into an agreement as to the number of weeks they will each apply for, or there is a court order respecting the sharing of those weeks`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST share THEN
        CONSIDER `reg 76.21(3) the most weeks that may be paid to the claimant` election
                     `A, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(4)(b)(i) of the Act when the weeks of benefits are divided`
                     `B, the number of weeks of provincial benefits that are paid to the provincial applicant`
                     `C, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii) of the Act`
                     `D, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) of the Act`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST cap THEN
            -- (4)'s 35 is D and its 61 is C.
            JUST (min share (min cap (`reg 76.21(4) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to the claimant in accordance with the election`
                                          election
                                          `D, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) of the Act`
                                          `C, the maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii) of the Act`)))
